        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12972156?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC proposes to add support for instrumenting function calls using mcount fentry or xray, and adding a new builtin attribute to toggle instrumentation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Today, mcount and xray enjoy experimental support, but I was unable to find any RFC proposing their inclusion.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/pmur/rfcs/blob/murp/instrumented-functions/text/0000-instrumented-functions.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3917",
            "title": "RFC: Add compiler support for instrumenting functions",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-11T22:52:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-02-10T16:18:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "pmur",
                "url": "https://github.com/pmur"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128289787?u=3cffcb544ac593c4daadd786263ecf02dc84df1a&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC proposes two new forms of method call syntax for method name disambiguation that keep the receiver on the left and preserve chaining. In doing so, it takes a step towards making implicit selection between trait methods and inherent implementations optional.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">An example of a chain of calls using proposed syntax:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"obj\n    .Self::chain()\n    .&lt;Trait1&gt;::of()\n    .&lt;Trait2&gt;::method()\n    .&lt;Trait1&gt;::calls();\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">obj\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">Self</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">::</span>chain<span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span>&lt;<span class=\"pl-c1\">Trait1</span>&gt;<span class=\"pl-kos\">::</span><span class=\"pl-en\">of</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span>&lt;<span class=\"pl-v\">Trait2</span>&gt;<span class=\"pl-kos\">::</span><span class=\"pl-en\">method</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span>&lt;<span class=\"pl-v\">Trait1</span>&gt;<span class=\"pl-kos\">::</span><span class=\"pl-en\">calls</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-important\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg class=\"octicon octicon-report mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0 1.75C0 .784.784 0 1.75 0h12.5C15.216 0 16 .784 16 1.75v9.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.25 13H8.06l-2.573 2.573A1.458 1.458 0 0 1 3 14.543V13H1.75A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25Zm1.75-.25a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v9.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h2a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.19l2.72-2.72a.749.749 0 0 1 .53-.22h6.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-9.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25Zm7 2.25v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 9a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z\"></path></svg>Important</p><p dir=\"auto\">When responding to RFCs, try to use inline review comments (it is possible to leave an inline review comment for the entire file at the top) instead of direct comments for normal comments and keep normal comments for procedural matters like starting FCPs.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This keeps the discussion more organized.</p>\n</div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/syudoer/rust-rfcs/blob/rfc2/text/3913-natural-method-disambiguation.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3913",
            "title": "RFC: Natural Method Disambiguation",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-11T08:28:12.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-27T18:22:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "syudoer",
                "url": "https://github.com/syudoer"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3050060?u=6ca85464b07c5464a052250a4fc3e3f9c03c97ed&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR introduces discussion about adding another derivable trait: <code class=\"notranslate\">Deref</code> (follows-up the newly added derivable trait <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3809\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3809/hovercard\"><code class=\"notranslate\">From</code></a>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/GuillaumeGomez/rfcs/blob/derive-deref/text/0000-derive-deref.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3911",
            "title": "Add `derive(Deref)` RFC",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-10T19:56:57.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-22T15:59:17.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "GuillaumeGomez",
                "url": "https://github.com/GuillaumeGomez"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33411204?u=2e161d32418071afd7547fe4c619134d386a4c97&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This is an RFC aimed at allowing Cargo to present client certificates when forming HTTP connections and support mutual TLS authentication with registries.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It is aimed at forming consensus around the discussion in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1229262351\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo/issues/10641\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/cargo/issues/10641/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo/issues/10641\">rust-lang/cargo#10641</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/matthague/rfcs/blob/master/text/3907-mtls-registry-authentication.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3907",
            "title": "Cargo mTLS registry authentication",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-21T05:09:19.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-17T03:24:34.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "matthague",
                "url": "https://github.com/matthague"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/134893?u=940724c499b98313ee519a69a725d26908685e6d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Let <code class=\"notranslate\">Option</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Box</code> derive <code class=\"notranslate\">#[must_use]</code> from their generic parameter <code class=\"notranslate\">T</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/dhardy/rfcs/blob/derive-must-use/text/0000-derive-must-use.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3906",
            "title": "Let `Option` derive `#[must_use]`",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-25T15:03:40.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-07T10:03:09.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dhardy",
                "url": "https://github.com/dhardy"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2280544?u=7f0df5aa9d0c05db41776dcfacedc8bbc2098746&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC proposes a general mechanism for version-based conditional compilation called \"typed cfgs\".</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This RFC proposes \"typed <code class=\"notranslate\">cfg</code>s\", a new form of conditional compilation predicate that understands types. Initially, this RFC proposes to add support for version-typed <code class=\"notranslate\">cfg</code>s, allowing for ergonomic version comparisons against the <em>language version</em> supported by the compiler. This would be exposed through two new built-in <code class=\"notranslate\">cfg</code> names:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">rust_version</code>, which can be compared against a language version literal, e.g., <code class=\"notranslate\">#[cfg(rust_version &gt;= \"1.85\")]</code>.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">rust_edition</code>, which can be compared against an edition literal, e.g., <code class=\"notranslate\">#[cfg(rust_edition &gt;= \"2024\")]</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This design solves a long-standing problem of conditionally compiling code for different Rust versions without requiring build scripts or forcing libraries to increase their Minimum Supported Rust Version (MSRV). It also replaces the <code class=\"notranslate\">cfg(version(..))</code> part of RFC 2523.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">History</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There have been several previous attempts to solve the problem of conditional compilation by Rust version.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>RFC <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"349785964\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/2523\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/2523/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/2523\">#2523</a> introduced <code class=\"notranslate\">#[cfg(version(..))]</code>. However, it left the syntax as an open question. Attempts to stabilize it were blocked because the new syntax would be a hard error on older compilers, defeating the goal of supporting older MSRVs.</li>\n<li>RFC <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3419220889\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3857\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3857/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3857\">#3857</a> proposed <code class=\"notranslate\">#[cfg(version_since(rust, ...))]</code>, which solved the MSRV problem and generalized the mechanism beyond Rust versions while defining the interaction with command line flags like <code class=\"notranslate\">--check-cfg</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This RFC takes the lessons from both previous attempts. It proposes a path to the ergonomic <code class=\"notranslate\">rust_version &gt;= \"...\"</code> syntax that was preferred during language team discussions, while providing a clear MSRV-compatibility story from day one.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The RFC also incorporates use cases from the <code class=\"notranslate\">cfg_target_version</code> RFC (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2760748965\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3750\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3750/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3750\">#3750</a>), which proposed a way to compare against the version of the target platform's SDK (e.g., <code class=\"notranslate\">#[cfg(target_version(macos &gt;= \"10.15\"))]</code>). Version-typed cfgs provide a path to supporting these comparions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Finally, it takes cues from previous discussions around <a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/pre-rfc-mutually-excusive-global-features/19618\" rel=\"nofollow\">mutually exclusive features</a> and a <code class=\"notranslate\">cfg_value!()</code> macro, and lays out a path toward more single-valued config types that could support these features.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/tmandry/rfcs/blob/cfg-version-typed/text/0000-version-typed-cfgs.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3905",
            "title": "Version-typed cfgs",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-19T22:58:01.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-07T02:39:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "tmandry",
                "url": "https://github.com/tmandry"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173050347?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/HackingRepo/rfcs/blob/patch-1/text/0000-trait-permits.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3903",
            "title": "RFC: Trait Implementation Privacy with `permits`",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-28T10:01:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-03T14:36:25.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "HackingRepo",
